## 2. CMY 2.0: Universal 4-Archetype Mathematical Kernel

To hit **99.9% geometric accuracy on ANY mesh** while keeping editability at `< 10` human curves + `< 12` HDA sliders, upgrade CMY into **one unified 3-color language backed by four mathematical archetypes**:

```
ANY COMPONENT  --->  Structural Mode Selector (Automatic + 1-click Override in Hub)
                        |
                        +--> Mode A: SYMMETRIC / CURVED PLATE     (Arm_Cuff, Car_Hood, Fender)
                        +--> Mode B: ASYMMETRIC / MULTI-PATCH CAD (Arm_Flare, Headlight, Trim)
                        +--> Mode C: CLOSED ORGANIC TUBE / BODY   (Torso, Limb, Hand, Dragon)
                        +--> Mode D: BRANCHING SKELETON & FOLIAGE (Tree Trunk, Horns, Roots)
```

### Universal Semantics of Cyan, Magenta, Yellow in CMY 2.0

1. **CYAN (`C`) = Skeleton / Harmonic Flow Graph (Longitudinal Parameter `u`)**
   - **Modes A & B (Shells / Plates)**: Replace single harmonic gradient with **Boundary-Conforming Multi-Block Harmonic Quadrangulation / Medial Axis Partition (`Straight Skeleton / Cross-Field`)**:
     - Instead of forcing 1 strip over a multi-pronged outline like `Arm_Flare`, detect reflex/concave notches (`angle > 210 deg`) and insert **Topological Saddle Cuts** along the Medial Axis (`scikit-fmm` distance transform ridge!).
     - This decomposes ANY arbitrary 2D silhouette (even with holes!) into a small graph of **clean 4-sided (or 3/5-sided Tarini) patches** (`Patch 1: Main Elbow`, `Patch 2: Upper Ear`, `Patch 3: Front Horn`, `Patch 4: Rear Wing`).
     - Solve an independent harmonic scalar field `nabla^2 u = 0`, `nabla^2 v = 0` inside each patch with `u in [0, 1]`, `v in [0, 1]` -> guaranteed **zero-crossing streamlines** that flow smoothly around EVERY hole and concave corner!
   - **Modes C & D (Closed Organic & Trees)**: Cyan is the **3D Piecewise Cubic Bezier Skeleton Curve `S(u)`** (parallel-transport / Bishop rotation-minimizing frame `(T(u), N(u), B(u))` so limbs/branches NEVER suffer Frenet inflection flipping!).

2. **MAGENTA (`M`) = Cross-Section Profile & Volumetric Wrap Rings (Transverse Parameter `v`)**
   - **What Magenta represents in 3D**: Cross-sectional closed loops (`Mode C/D`) or open transverse arcs (`Mode A/B`) attached along `u` in local Bishop frame `(N(u), B(u))`:
     $$R(u, \theta) = R_0(u) \cdot \Big(1 + e(u)\cos(2(\theta - \alpha(u))) + \text{wrap\_bend}(u, \theta)\Big) + \text{crease\_bump}(u, \theta)$$
   - **Multi-View Triangulation Lock**: Instead of guessing depth solely from 1 view, whenever >= 2 views exist (`front`, `left`, `top`), triangulate exact `(x(u, v), y(u, v), z(u, v))` intersection rays (`Cameras.py` ALREADY achieves `2.3e-15 m` precision!) so front+left+top silhouettes constrain both **Centerline Depth (`Z`)** AND **Cross-Section Eccentricity / Wrap Angle** simultaneously!
   - **Asymmetric Outer + Inner Profiles (Solves `Arm_Flare`!)**: Mode B decouples `M_outer(u, v)` (outer sculpted surface facing camera) from `M_inner(u, v)` (inner thickness offset OR true reconstructed `back` view profile), instead of forcing `z_back = -z_front`!

3. **YELLOW (`Y`) = Feature Curve Graph with Per-Vertex Crease Profile (`Crease / Ridge / Valley / Fold`)**
   - **Upgraded Feature Representation**: Each Yellow curve `Y_k` is NOT just a fixed row `row=0` or X-column pixel path:
     - Stored as a **parametric UV/surface spline `(u(s), v(s))`** embedded directly inside the patch/tube topology (or edge-loop aligned via **Snake / Tridiagonal Constraint** so patch edges snap cleanly ONTO Yellow ridges!).
     - Carries explicit per-vertex vectors: `(kind: crisp | smooth | valley | fold, weight_0_1: float, width_px: float, amplitude: float, bevel_radius: float)`.
     - **Pin-Exact Sharpness**: `weight` drives OpenSubdiv `creaseweight` directly (`RunCmy.py:83` ALREADY validates variable vertex `f@creaseweight`, once isolated cleanly from inner faces!).

